格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"中文版请阅读 README.zh.md.","id":"gh:1339449291","install_available":true,"language":"Python","name":"dsh-on-imessage","slug":"yuunnn/dsh-on-imessage","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"中文版请阅读 README.zh.md."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-on-iMessage"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> Chat with your local DeepSeek Harness (dsh) agents from your iPhone, right inside the Messages app"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" — no extra apps, no servers, no cloud."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**中文版请阅读 README.zh.md.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Turn your Mac into a 24/7 dsh companion that lives in your iMessage threads. Send a message to your "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"bridge account and your local dsh agent picks it up, switches workspaces/sessions, runs tools, and r"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"eplies back — all without opening a terminal."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Why This Exists"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- You already live in iMessage; dsh lives on your Mac.\n- SSH from your phone is clunky. Web UIs need"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" ports/VPNs. Telegram/WeChat need third-party platforms.\n- iMessage is already on every iPhone, end-"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"to-end encrypted, and works offline-first."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"This bridge gives you a **real chat experience**: white bubbles from dsh, blue bubbles from you, one"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"dge gives you a **real chat experience**: white bubbles from dsh, blue bubbles from you, one-to-one."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **Chat with dsh from iMessage** — send any message, get the agent's reply.\n- **Workspace switching"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"** — `dsh`, `dsh use stockKing`, `dsh use 2`.\n- **Session switching** — `dsh sessions stockKing`, `d"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"sh use stockKing 0`.\n- **New sessions** — `dsh new <message>`.\n- **Web UI sync** — when dsh web is r"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"unning, messages go through its local API so your browser stays in sync.\n- **Safe by default** — str"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ict sender whitelist; nobody else can trigger your agent.\n- **Bilingual replies** — follows your Mac"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"'s language (or `DSH_BRIDGE_LANG=en|zh`).\n- **Zero third-party services** — everything stays on your"},{"id":"p10s7","text":" Mac and Apple's iMessage."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- macOS with Messages (iMessage) and a second Apple ID for the bridge account (recommended, avoids s"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"elf-chat duplication).\n- DeepSeek Harness installed (this is the `dsh` agent).\n- Python 3.9+ (stdlib"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" only for the bridge)."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Option A — as a dsh plugin (recommended)"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"This repo is a standard DeepSeek Harness plugin bundle, so it can be installed with one command:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Then set the required environment variables in the shell that starts `dsh web`:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Restart `dsh web`. The plugin starts `bridge.py` automatically when the dsh profile boots."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"> If pnpm asks to allow build scripts, add `dsh-on-imessage: true` to the profile's `pnpm-workspace."},{"id":"p20s2","text":"yaml` — this package has no build step, so this is usually not needed."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Option B — standalone daemon"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Paste this into your Mac terminal:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"That's it. The installer clones this repo into `~/.dsh/bridges/imessage`, starts the daemon, and **p"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"rints the next steps, including signing in to a second Apple ID in Messages**."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"> The installer only needs `git` and `python3`. Everything else is already on your Mac."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"**DSH_BIN** (optional): if your dsh CLI is not on PATH and not in the npx cache, set the environment"},{"id":"p26s2","text":" variable to its entry point, e.g. `export DSH_BIN=\"$HOME/deepseek-harness/apps/cli/lib/bin.js\"`."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Setup"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"1. **Create a second Apple ID** (e.g. `dsh@example.com`) at appleid.apple.com. This becomes the \"dsh"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" persona\".\n2. **Sign in to that account in Mac Messages** (Messages > Settings > iMessage).\n3. **Set"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" the bridge configuration**. The bridge reads these from the environment:\n- `DSH_BUDDY` = your iPhon"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"e number, e.g. `+861234567890`\n- `DSH_AUTHORIZED_FROM` = your iPhone number (or the email you reply "},{"id":"p28s5","text":"from)\n- `DSH_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT` = the iMessage account the bridge listens on, e.g. `E:dsh@icloud.com`\n4"},{"id":"p28s6","text":". **Restart the daemon**:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"5. **Text your bridge account** from your iPhone. It replies with `dsh` help."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Usage"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| Command | Meaning |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| `dsh` | List workspaces |\n| `dsh use <id\\|path\\|name>` | Switch workspace (latest session) |\n| `ds"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"h use <id\\|path\\|name> <session#>` | Switch workspace + specific session |\n| `dsh sessions [<workspa"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"ce>]` | List sessions |\n| `dsh new <message>` | Start a new session |\n| anything else | Continue the"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"ons |\n| `dsh new <message>` | Start a new session |\n| anything else | Continue the current session |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Workspaces are matched by index, full path, or basename — exact match wins, ambiguous matches list c"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" are matched by index, full path, or basename — exact match wins, ambiguous matches list candidates."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"- **Sender whitelist**: only `AUTHORIZED_FROM` handles are processed.\n- **Account isolation**: only "},{"id":"p38s2","text":"messages addressed to the bridge account are processed.\n- **Local-only**: no public servers, no tele"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"metry, no cloud.\n- You can keep using iMessage for personal memos; those go to a different thread an"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"d.\n- You can keep using iMessage for personal memos; those go to a different thread and are ignored."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## FAQ"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"**Why a second Apple ID?** iMessage treats messages between addresses of the same Apple ID as self-c"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"hat, which duplicates bubbles. A separate Apple ID gives a clean one-to-one conversation."},{"id":"p41s1","text":"**Do I need the dsh web UI running?** No. The bridge falls back to the headless CLI if the web proce"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"ss is not listening."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"**Can other people trigger it?** No. Only your whitelisted handle(s) can."},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Apache-2.0. See LICENSE."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
